Third-party components (retained with their own licenses and notices):

1. OpenLine Wallet (github.com/terryncew/openline-wallet)
   The backend imports the openline_wallet Python package from the vendored
   snapshot in backend/vendor/ (Apache-2.0, see
   backend/vendor/openline-wallet-LICENSE.txt and backend/vendor/VENDOR.md
   for the source commit). All mandate grants, revocations, bundle admissions,
   challenge issuance, exact-action evaluations, and signed gate receipts are
   produced by that package's ReferenceGate/EffectGate and Wallet classes.
   The workshop adds no authorization logic of its own.

2. OpenLine Claim Graph (vendored in backend/vendor/openline_claim_graph/)
   MIT license, Copyright (c) 2026 Terrynce White (see
   backend/vendor/openline-claim-graph-LICENSE.txt).

3. diorama-builder (github.com/hitesh153/diorama-builder, MIT, Hitesh Goyal)
   Inspected as a rendering reference on 2026-09-25. Not vendored; no code,
   branding, or assets used.

4. claude-office (github.com/paulrobello/claude-office, MIT, Paul Robello)
   Inspected as an event/hook reference on 2026-09-25. Its documented
   hook-to-event mapping approach informed the CONNECTED adapter design.
   Not vendored; no code, branding, or assets used.

5. Claude Code hooks reference (code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks)
   Public documentation used to define the CONNECTED adapter's accepted
   event names and redaction policy.

Assets: all 3D geometry is procedural code in frontend/src/world/scene/.
No bundled fonts (system font stacks only), no image/texture assets beyond
favicon.svg and icons.svg, no third-party models. An unreferenced image
asset (frontend/src/assets/hero.png, origin unknown) was removed from the
distribution rather than shipped under an uncertain license.
